    "description": "Layer-2 guarded SQL: run exactly one SELECT statement against the flowleap.* semantic views (?section=semantic-model is the catalog; ?section=examples has verified question→SQL pairs). Deterministic gate: parse check, flowleap-only relation allowlist, EXPLAIN cost bands (warn > 1.5M cost — query runs with a warning; reject > 5M), a 5,000-row cap enforced as a hard error (never truncation), a 5MB response cap, and a 20s statement timeout. Use for aggregate questions no Layer-1 endpoint covers; check `promoted_to` in ?section=examples first.",
    "errorEnvelope": {
      "cases": [
        {
          "code": "patstat_sql_invalid",
          "recovery": "Send exactly one SELECT statement. Use details.position and the parser message to fix the syntax; resubmit once with retryOf.",
          "status": 400,
          "when": "The SQL failed to parse, contained multiple statements, or is not a plain SELECT (details.reason: parse_error | multiple_statements | not_select)."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_sql_forbidden",
          "recovery": "Schema-qualify every table as flowleap.<view> using only the views in ?section=semantic-model; resubmit once with retryOf.",
          "status": 403,
          "when": "A referenced relation is outside the flowleap schema, or a table name is unqualified (details.relations names the offenders)."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_sql_error",
          "recovery": "Fix the SQL using position/hint against the semantic model, resubmit once with retryOf. Do not retry unchanged.",
          "status": 400,
          "when": "Postgres rejected the statement at planning time — undefined column, type mismatch, etc. (details: sqlstate, position, hint, detail)."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_sql_too_expensive",
          "recovery": "Narrow the query — tighter year range or applicant filter, or aggregate instead of listing rows. NEVER retry unchanged.",
          "status": 422,
          "when": "The plan's estimated cost exceeds the reject ceiling, or the gate's own 2s EXPLAIN timed out (details: estimated_cost, cost_ceiling)."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_sql_timeout",
          "recovery": "THE ONE ERROR WORTH AN IDENTICAL RETRY (#402): the tables are far larger than the cache, so a cold call can time out where the same SQL succeeds warm. Resubmit it UNCHANGED once with retryOf; only if that also times out, narrow it (a year floor, a tighter anchor) or use /v1/patstat/portfolio. CHECK YOUR CLIENT FIRST — the FlowLeap CLI resends any 5xx twice on its own, so a 504 that reaches you through it has already had its retry and should be narrowed, not resent.",
          "status": 504,
          "when": "The query passed the cost gate but hit the 20s execution timeout (details.timeout_ms)."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_sql_too_many_rows",
          "recovery": "Aggregate the result, add ORDER BY with LIMIT ≤ 5000, or select fewer columns; resubmit once with retryOf.",
          "status": 422,
          "when": "The result exceeded the 5,000-row cap, or the 5MB response cap (the message distinguishes). Hard error — results are never truncated."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_busy",
          "recovery": "Honor the Retry-After header and back off — this is load, NOT a problem with your SQL. Do not rewrite the query.",
          "status": 503,
          "when": "All guarded-SQL slots are busy and the 5s queue expired."
        },
        {
          "code": "subscription_required",
          "recovery": "Tell the user their FlowLeap subscription is inactive — nothing to fix in the SQL.",
          "status": 402,
          "when": "The account has no active or trialing subscription (fires before the route runs)."
        },
        {
          "code": "rate_limited",
          "recovery": "Honor Retry-After and pause — batch questions into fewer, better queries rather than looping.",
          "status": 429,
          "when": "Over the dedicated 10 requests/minute guarded-SQL budget for this user."
        },
        {
          "code": "patstat_unavailable",
          "recovery": "Use the Layer-1 endpoints or the other patent-data routes; do not retry.",
          "status": 503,
          "when": "The guarded-SQL layer is not configured on this deployment (no PATSTAT_AGENT_DATABASE_URL)."
        }
      ],
      "description": "Gate failures are typed; the message always carries the underlying parser/Postgres detail plus a recovery line. Every patstat_sql_* error is retryable-by-rewrite: fix the SQL once, resubmit with `retryOf`, and stop after a second failure. ONE EXCEPTION — patstat_sql_timeout is retryable UNCHANGED (once), because a cold cache and a too-heavy query fail the same way (#402).",
      "shape": "{ success: false, error: { code: string, message: string, ...details }, status: integer }"
    },
    "method": "POST",
    "note": "Follow the guarded-sql workflow: one informed retry per error, then stop. Apply the interpretation_conventions block from ?section=semantic-model and always state the chosen interpretation alongside data_edition.",
    "params": {
      "question": {
        "description": "The user's natural-language question, verbatim (≤1,000 chars, truncated). Audit-only — always send it: it feeds the query-review pipeline that turns good queries into verified examples.",
        "example": "Where does Siemens hold the most inventions?",
        "required": false,
        "type": "string"
      },
      "retryOf": {
        "description": "Correlation marker linking a retry to the rejected attempt it fixes. Audit-only. Send on every retry.",
        "required": false,
        "type": "string"
      },
      "sql": {
        "description": "Exactly one SELECT statement. Every table must be schema-qualified as flowleap.<view> (unqualified names are rejected). Un-LIMITed SQL is allowed — the row cap is enforced server-side.",
        "example": "SELECT office, COUNT(DISTINCT family_id) AS inventions FROM flowleap.applications a JOIN flowleap.applicants ap ON ap.application_id = a.application_id WHERE UPPER(ap.name) LIKE 'SIEMENS%' GROUP BY office ORDER BY inventions DESC",
        "required": true,
        "type": "string"
      }
    },
    "path": "/v1/patstat/query",
    "rateLimitNote": "Dedicated budget: 10 requests/minute per user (separate from other patent-data routes). Responses are NOT cached.",
    "responseShape": "{ success: true, rows: object[], rowCount: integer, data_edition: string, warnings?: [{ code: \"patstat_sql_expensive\", message, details: { cost, warn_threshold, reject_ceiling } }] }"
  }
}

